feat(profile): add a Chat ID row with tap-to-copy

Shows the numeric id of the open peer on its profile screen. A tap copies
it and shows a "copied" bulletin. The value uses the Bot API form: users
and bots use the user id, secret chats show the other user's id, basic
groups use -chat_id, and supergroups and channels use
-1000000000000 - channel_id (the "-100" form). Forum topics show the
parent chat id.

Formatting lives in org.telegram.myclient.ChatIdHelper. ProfileActivity
only gets the row wiring: field, row index, view type, bind, click and
diff position.
